  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSum of first 100 terms, S₁₀₀ = 50\n\nSum of first 200 terms, S₂₀₀ = 90\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nSum of first n terms of an A.P: S_n = (n)/(2) [2a + (n - 1)d]\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nS₁₀₀ = (100)/(2) [2a + 99d] = 50 ⇒ 50 × [2a + 99d] = 50 ⇒ 2a + 99d = 1 ... (i)\n\nS₂₀₀ = (200)/(2) [2a + 199d] = 90 ⇒ 100 × [2a + 199d] = 90 ⇒ 2a + 199d = 0.9 ... (ii)\n\nSubtract (i) from (ii): (2a + 199d) - (2a + 99d) = 0.9 - 1 ⇒ 100d = -0.1 ⇒ d = -0.001\n\nSubstitute in (i): 2a + 99(–0.001) = 1 ⇒ 2a – 0.099 = 1 ⇒ 2a = 1.099 ⇒ a = 0.5495\n\nNow find S₃₀₀:\n\nS₃₀₀ = (300)/(2) [2a + 299d] ⇒ 150 × [2 × 0.5495 + 299 × (–0.001)]\n\n⇒ 150 × [1.099 – 0.299] = 150 × 0.8 = 120\n\n**∴ The correct answer is: 120**",
